  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAD4COVID</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic, Ghana has adopted a comprehensive testing strategy. Currently, Ghana is focussing on containing the spread of the disease by tracing, testing, treating, as well as restricting movement/travel. However, restriction of movement is challenging in a country like Ghana where many live day-to-day and in densely populated households, making &#x2018;stocking up&#x2019; and self-isolation virtually impossible, which will force people to go outside, increasing the risk of the COVID-19 spread. To support decentralized triage testing with X-ray, 55 facilities across Ghana have gained access to the CAD4COVID software, which have been installed by Delft Imaging in Ghana thanks to the financial support by DGGF TA. The X-ray systems installed as part of an ORIO project were previously placed across the country. The X-ray systems were paired with CAD4TB, in order to accelerate the detection of tuberculosis. The pre-existing X-ray systems have been enhanced with CAD4COVID to build a first-line infrastructure to face COVID-19. In the period until December 2020 already 14.000 people have been screened. Due to this project 4 direct and 2 indirect jobs have been supported in Ghana. A total of 117 people spread amongst the 55 healthcare facilities have been trained to use and install the software.</narrative>
  </description>
